// OpenMap's public API (`OpenMapAPI`, major 1) and Blizzard's map frame it hosts in (`WorldMapFrame`), as
// `openMap.lua` reads them: neither is declared by the client's API. OpenMap is MIT; it is called, never copied.
import Client from "$client"

// Whether OpenMap is there and of the API this reads (major 1, version 4 or later).
public function present(): Boolean
// The world map's canvas, where pins stand; nil before Blizzard's map is made.
public function canvas(): any Client.Frame | nil
// The map the world map shows (`WorldMapFrame:GetMapID()`); 0 while it doesn't show.
public function shownMap(): Integer
// Whether OpenMap's stitched map shows now.
public function stitched(): Boolean
// Where a point of a map, 0 to 1, is on the canvas while stitched: on the map the stitched view stands on, outside 0
// to 1 where it is off it; nil where OpenMap can't say (the map isn't part of the stitched world).
public function canvasOf(map: Integer, x: Number, y: Number): (Number | nil, Number | nil)
// The highest frame level OpenMap's art takes on the canvas: pins stand over it.
public function artTop(): Integer
// `run` is called when the world map shows or hides, when the map it shows changes, and when OpenMap's view moves
// or its stitched map comes or goes. Once; `forget` takes it away.
public function listen(run: () => nil)
public function forget()
// A switch in OpenMap's menu, under «Ordaen»: what it shows comes from `get`, a click calls `set`.
public function menuToggle(id: String, label: String, get: () => Boolean, set: (on: Boolean) => nil)
// The game's tooltip beside a pin: its first line the title, in white, the others under it.
public function tip(owner: any Client.Frame, lines: Array<String>)
public function untip()
